E8.2  Reachable market
  Si       delivers process heat up to 45 degC
  SiC-300  delivers process heat up to 280 degC
  SiC-max  delivers process heat up to 445 degC
  US process heat below 300 degC: 8010 TBtu of 11000 (73%), a continuous 268 GW
  refineries: 62% of process heat (1380 TBtu) lies at 100-300 degC
  steam cracking: the pyrolysis section (65% of cracker energy) runs at 750 degC or more
  energy per tonne (DOE bandwidth, onsite): ethylene 16.4 GJ; HDPE 2.41, LLDPE 2.03, LDPE 2.66, PP 1.43 GJ
  polymerisation needs 9-16% of the energy of cracking per unit mass
  the below-300 degC band could absorb the heat of 268 GW of furnace computation;
  furnace heat does not lack buyers at any foreseeable scale

E8.2b The refinery
  US refineries burn 3375 TBtu of fuel a year; 65% of it is their own byproduct gas
  1380 TBtu of refinery process heat (62%) lies at 100-300 degC, within the design's reach
  supplying it from computation frees at least 1380 TBtu of fuel a year, 41% of refinery fuel use,
  and avoids at least 73 Mt of CO2; it is the heat of 46 GW of computation
  the refinery then makes the same products while burning less of its own output:
  the hydrocarbons it no longer burns for heat remain available as product

